Package: tuxindrive-network-lab
Version: 0.26.31+lab5
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: TuxInDrive contributors <tpluharik@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-cryptography, python3-defusedxml, python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, xdg-utils
Homepage: https://github.com/tpluharik/TuxInDrive
Description: Isolated TuxInDrive server and client networking scenario lab
 TuxInDrive Network Lab runs production protocol code against a loopback-only,
 ephemeral server and fictional clients. Its visual topology shows actual
 multi-address loopback traffic. It automatically tests authentication,
 tenant isolation, opaque mailbox/object/rendezvous/collaboration operations,
 invalid inputs, concurrency, observability and restart durability. It never
 loads real cloud accounts, production client configuration or synchronized
 folders. Results are shown in a separate resizable window and private logs.
